Z||000000||Gokart||07-29-2000||07:42 AM||||Could someone pull out their trunk light for me and tell me how the wiring is supposed to go! I bought one from alpha and it is just the light assembly only and I'm missing the plug from my wires to plug into it. I'll crimp on some connectors to the wires but which one goes to the top of the light and which goes to the bottom? One wire is light orange in color and the other is white. TIA!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||alpha||07-29-2000||09:18 AM||||Marc,<P>I just checked my car regarding this. On it the orange wire goes to the terminal which goes to the oppisite side of the assembly from the plug. The white wire goes to the terminal which connects to the closer side of the bulb. I don't think it really matters which goes to which tho. That is because it is only a lightbulb and it is not grounded in any way. I hope that was the answer to the question you were asking. If not, just explain futher.<P>I should have included the wires from the switch. I just did not think you needed them and I think I threw them out when I was cleaning up.....they were cut when I did a fastback swap.<P>Anyways HTH and best of luck,<P>--Douglas Knight||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||07-29-2000||10:34 PM||||You did fine alpha cause you sent me just what I asked for! The wiring didn't work anyway. No power and don't know what the previous owner had done but I re-did my own. I spliced one of the wires that lights up the PONTIAC and got my power there. I like it cause now it only comes on if the lights are on(when else would you need it besides dark!)so I can leave the decklid open as long as needed with draining the battery or half to fool with that lever by the trunk lock <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Thanks alpha!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
